Code Contracts is a powerful tool that helps you write robust, bug-free code by specifying preconditions, postconditions, and invariants. These conditions are not only verified at compile time, but also at runtime, ensuring that you are following the contract of your methods.

To use Generic.List in Code Contracts, you need to have a test method that makes use of the Generic.List. This method will serve as the target method for the Code Contracts analysis. Let's assume we have the following Generic.List:

